@title INC-3302: Late nightly sales reports
@subtitle Postmortem, incident date 2026-10-06
@author Data Platform team
@date 2026-10-06

kpi Reports late | 8 h 40 min | due 03:00 UTC, sent 11:40 | bad
kpi Store managers affected | 214 | empty or stale reports | bad
kpi Backfill | 95 min | neutral

## Summary

The point-of-sale vendor added a column named `tender_subtype` to the sales feed without notice. The ingestion job failed on it. The failure alert went to a retired channel, so nobody knew until a store manager asked why the report was empty.

## Timeline

All times UTC on 2026-10-06.

table = time,event; 01:15,Vendor deploys the schema change; 02:10,Ingestion job fails for the first time; 02:40,Retries exhausted; 03:00,Reports miss their deadline and no alert fires; 07:25,A store manager asks in #retail-ops why the report is empty; 07:50,Support pages the Data Platform on-call; 08:35,Cause identified; 09:20,Schema mapping patched; 10:05,Backfill starts; 11:40,Reports published

## Contributing factors

- The failure alert still routed to the retired channel #data-alerts-old.
- There was no schema contract check on vendor feeds.
- The backfill ran serially.

## What went well

- Once paged, the on-call found the cause in 45 minutes.
- No wrong numbers were published.

## Action items

step Route pipeline alerts to the on-call pager | 2026-10-16 | Samuel Achterberg
step Add a schema contract check on vendor feeds | 2026-11-06 | Lucia Fontaine
step Parallelize the backfill by partition | 2026-11-20 | Data Platform on-call
step Require 14 days' notice of feed changes in the vendor contract | 2026-10-30 | Vendor Management
